INSERT INTO `courses_prolearningquizquestion` VALUES ('0105828967d8472786d707aa49a34b86','Which of the following represents the most general form of a first-order differential equation as presented in the text?','mcq','[\"`y = mx + b`\", \"`F(x, y, dy/dx) = 0`\", \"`dy/dx + P(x) = Q(x)`\", \"`∫ y dx = C`\"]','1',NULL,1,4,'2025-10-10 04:22:14.205000','826bbc0263b34345b167ee6f0d969cab'),('08967dce7b39400184fda573a602fa18','In any right triangle, which side is always the longest?','mcq','[\"The Adjacent Side\", \"The Opposite Side\", \"The Hypotenuse\", \"The side next to the angle of reference\"]','2',NULL,1,2,'2025-10-08 11:47:29.010000','64a5ab1b9a8e4be3b8592d4fcbf8f20d'),('095941fd47754f87ae358212191eea15','Which of the following is an example of a \"side effect\" that the `useEffect` Hook enables functional components to perform?','mcq','[\"Managing internal component state.\", \"Declaring a new functional component.\", \"Data fetching.\", \"Changing component props.\"]','2',NULL,1,3,'2025-10-08 13:12:16.932000','c07d62f459584f95ae7f68eeb706d841'),('0decc4da0e5a4ff5a11d92a6831bab7b','What is the primary benefit of \"Props\" in relation to component reusability?','mcq','[\"They allow components to manage their own internal, changing data.\", \"They enable components to be static and unchanging.\", \"They allow the creation of generic components that can be customized by parent data.\", \"They ensure that components only display information based on internal logic.\"]','2',NULL,1,5,'2025-10-08 13:12:16.854000','ff8aac3e77954f00aa8104edb373050c'),('0e4edf52e550438eb2fd6e31f265f14c','Which of the following best describes Python as a programming language?','mcq','[\"Low-level and compiled\", \"High-level and interpreted\", \"Low-level and interpreted\", \"High-level and compiled\"]','1',NULL,1,2,'2025-09-18 15:47:10.047000','5a37bdf1b08e450a873e7a3f08f960ec'),('0ff8b469f460408a8b728088b13c4c24','Which side of a right triangle is always the longest?','mcq','[\"The Opposite Side\", \"The Adjacent Side\", \"The Hypotenuse\", \"The side next to the acute angle\"]','2',NULL,1,5,'2025-10-08 11:51:31.650000','1a3b7e637fb445fa9d533dc78e3a6ced'),('1352bc99dc3f4ecba4a82bd9d40b274e','In Django\'s Model-View-Template (MTV) architecture, what is the primary responsibility of the **Model**?','mcq','[\"To receive web requests and return HTTP responses.\", \"To define the data structure, handle data storage, retrieval, and validation.\", \"To display the user interface and present data.\", \"To manage project-wide settings and configurations.\"]','1',NULL,1,5,'2025-10-08 16:49:32.805000','ab9fc04dfb08474b81448a4cd33f8167'),('153f29668cf9460bb2335693b404442a','What is Node.js primarily described as in the provided content?','mcq','[\"A new JavaScript framework for frontend development.\", \"A database management system.\", \"A JavaScript runtime environment.\", \"A web browser.\"]','2',NULL,1,1,'2025-10-08 13:17:37.685000','2942df64080146d4b8ed6664c0ad1698'),('167ba17fe0a74ba2b550e511d3019748','Which of the following is a key characteristic of a \"Linear\" ODE, according to the text?','mcq','[\"The coefficients of y and its derivatives must be constant.\", \"The unknown function y and its derivatives appear only to the first power and are not multiplied together.\", \"The equation must have at least three terms.\", \"The independent variable must appear to the first power.\"]','1',NULL,1,4,'2025-10-10 04:22:14.284000','0a43196b3ca94ea9b55f955d79081eb5'),('167d7255741f44e8aa9868fed9bddbf4','What type of patterns does trigonometry primarily help us understand and predict, as described in the text?','mcq','[\"Random, unpredictable events.\", \"Linear, non-repeating sequences.\", \"Predictable, cyclical patterns.\", \"Static, unchanging measurements.\"]','2',NULL,1,3,'2025-10-10 08:28:03.953685','71afc962f2104a6abeb7d480f6c4dd80'),('17500772130445cd8cb49e859b9077de','In a right triangle, which side is always the longest and is located opposite the 90-degree angle?','mcq','[\"The Adjacent Side\", \"The Opposite Side\", \"The Hypotenuse\", \"The Base\"]','2',NULL,1,2,'2025-10-08 12:07:50.558000','670b202c2b2c48afb3656a5d17357b9f'),('177e6015b784498bb7571dbb0013cb87','What defines one radian?','mcq','[\"The angle formed by an arc length equal to the circle\'s diameter.\", \"The angle formed at the center by an arc length equal to the circle\'s radius.\", \"The angle formed by a full circle divided by pi.\", \"The angle formed by 180 degrees.\"]','1',NULL,1,1,'2025-10-10 08:28:03.771742','3923bddcbc8a412fae18621ffcdbbd4c'),('1bdb6186a608443e9b8c4613bffa41e7','Which of the following equations is an example of a First-Order Ordinary Differential Equation, based on the provided definition?','mcq','[\"∂y/∂x + ∂y/∂t = 0\", \"d²y/dx² + dy/dx = x\", \"dy/dx = 2x\", \"y = 2x + 5\"]','2',NULL,1,5,'2025-10-10 04:12:08.152000','90d62550c0d54237947475f5e801a6f6'),('1d028237f01241bb899818d60d6668da','Which two sides of a right triangle form the 90-degree angle?','mcq','[\"The Hypotenuse and the Opposite Side\", \"The Hypotenuse and the Adjacent Side\", \"The two Legs\", \"The Opposite Side and the Adjacent Side (regardless of reference angle)\"]','2',NULL,1,4,'2025-10-10 08:28:03.606868','d9c56dcdae694234b4c12ff647854293'),('1d4af467986f40ae8afff08795d85cba','What is the primary purpose of Right Triangle Trigonometry as described in the text?','mcq','[\"To study the history of mathematics.\", \"To find unknown sides and angles of right-angled triangles.\", \"To design abstract art.\", \"To measure the temperature of objects.\"]','1',NULL,1,1,'2025-10-08 11:51:31.641000','1a3b7e637fb445fa9d533dc78e3a6ced'),('1e9188efc8824c9183ac1a95d36a378a','What is the defining characteristic of a right triangle?','mcq','[\"All three angles are equal.\", \"It contains one angle that measures exactly 90 degrees.\", \"All sides are of equal length.\", \"It has no angles greater than 45 degrees.\"]','1',NULL,1,1,'2025-10-08 12:07:50.556000','670b202c2b2c48afb3656a5d17357b9f'),('1f5f2f6010d74e78a3ace5fae1ed0277','What is the defining characteristic of a right triangle?','mcq','[\"All its angles are acute.\", \"It has one angle exactly equal to 90 degrees.\", \"All its sides are equal in length.\", \"It has two angles that are equal.\"]','1',NULL,1,1,'2025-10-08 13:06:29.629000','688bcdacc17b4a498892e9e76f9327ae'),('21674445c23041f3aa4a612d5e409381','How is 1 radian defined?','mcq','[\"The angle formed by an arc length equal to 360 degrees.\", \"The angle formed when the diameter of a circle is wrapped around its circumference.\", \"The angle formed by an arc length equal to the circle\'s radius.\", \"The angle that measures exactly 1 degree.\"]','2',NULL,1,3,'2025-10-08 11:51:31.733000','759235b9d57a406fb2d43c1b09ddb086'),('23df9680c9e8417a9b4deb482abae290','In a right triangle, which side is always the longest and is directly across from the 90-degree angle?','mcq','[\"The Adjacent Side\", \"The Opposite Side\", \"The Hypotenuse\", \"The Base\"]','2',NULL,1,2,'2025-10-08 17:01:49.734000','a7fb522bd62546d9b06810a8c5579b76'),('2485db4888df47edabc329f28476b845','According to the text, what is a primary reason First-Order Differential Equations are indispensable?','mcq','[\"They describe static snapshots of systems.\", \"They provide exact future states without calculation.\", \"They model systems where the rate of change depends on the quantity itself, time, or both.\", \"They are only used in theoretical mathematics, not real-world scenarios.\"]','2',NULL,1,1,'2025-10-10 04:22:14.198000','826bbc0263b34345b167ee6f0d969cab'),('24b852f4efb14c588e1d514275701198','In the analogy provided, if a component is a \"small, specialized machine,\" what do \"Props\" represent?','mcq','[\"The internal memory or current working data of the machine.\", \"The tasks the machine performs.\", \"The configuration settings or ingredients fed into the machine from the outside.\", \"The output generated by the machine.\"]','2',NULL,1,3,'2025-10-08 13:12:16.853000','ff8aac3e77954f00aa8104edb373050c'),('25f18a920c0b4c3784df6bc6ffd40f71','Which fundamental mathematical concepts are mentioned as prerequisites for navigating the realm of differential equations?','mcq','[\"Linear algebra and discrete mathematics.\", \"Statistics and probability theory.\", \"Derivatives and integrals from calculus.\", \"Geometry and trigonometry.\"]','2',NULL,1,5,'2025-10-10 04:11:14.272000','aae4ce9acb1c4afeba814726a675d550'),('26f3998698cb497ab4e72afd61838839','The Laplace Transform converts a function of a real variable \'t\' (often time) into a function of which complex variable?','mcq','[\"x (space)\", \"y (amplitude)\", \"s (frequency)\", \"z (impedance)\"]','2',NULL,1,4,'2025-10-10 04:22:14.379000','580ab48eb18e4e8baee457a0401cc668'),('27ab8724dde74eecbbf83efbc78fd198','What does the term \"First-Order\" signify in a First-Order Ordinary Differential Equation?','mcq','[\"The equation is the simplest type of differential equation.\", \"The unknown function appears only once.\", \"The highest derivative present in the equation is the first derivative.\", \"The equation can only be solved using integration.\"]','2',NULL,1,3,'2025-10-10 04:12:08.148000','90d62550c0d54237947475f5e801a6f6'),('29f12192a3a34a64b47c01ea73e8abec','According to the content, what capability does the `useState` Hook provide to functional components?','mcq','[\"Performing \\\"side effects\\\" like data fetching.\", \"Managing and updating their own internal state.\", \"Interacting with the outside world directly.\", \"Defining custom lifecycle methods.\"]','1',NULL,1,2,'2025-10-08 13:12:16.931000','c07d62f459584f95ae7f68eeb706d841'),('2c42be114fd4416c985daeab295b8ee4','What is the key difference between declaring a variable with `let` versus `const`?','mcq','[\"`let` variables are global, while `const` variables are local.\", \"`let` allows the variable\'s value to be reassigned, while `const` declares a constant whose value cannot be reassigned.\", \"`const` variables can only store `number` data types, while `let` can store any type.\", \"`let` is an older keyword, while `const` is modern.\"]','1',NULL,1,4,'2025-10-08 13:25:59.716000','b5632b45519049c494b634084e77c2a8'),('30d839ac45284866a011a7df1a8a4422','Which of the following phenomena is NOT mentioned in the text as an application where first-order ODEs are indispensable?','mcq','[\"The spread of a disease.\", \"The growth of a population.\", \"The trajectory of a satellite in space.\", \"The decay of a radioactive substance.\"]','2',NULL,1,4,'2025-10-08 12:21:30.310000','1c18e83623634608a445f8410a760a8c'),('31537372f7524ca3b853a07eb17e488b','Which operator is used to assign a value to a variable in Python?','mcq','[\"`==`\", \"`+`\", \"`=`\", \"`:`\"]','2',NULL,1,2,'2025-10-08 17:16:38.116000','9cd0f04a76c145e783f5a5d9d16b9166'),('32080ac2589546368f92fff144f1ea57','According to the text, how is tan(x) defined in relation to sin(x) and cos(x)?','mcq','[\"tan(x) = cos(x) / sin(x)\", \"tan(x) = sin(x) * cos(x)\", \"tan(x) = sin(x) / cos(x)\", \"tan(x) = 1 / sin(x)\"]','2',NULL,1,5,'2025-10-10 08:28:04.159127','0b70b73bb0724d8ab38231710baff8ad'),('3398faded3504abb8bf30f4d9cb95f2f','In any right triangle, which side is always the longest?','mcq','[\"The Opposite side\", \"The Adjacent side\", \"The Hypotenuse\", \"The 90-degree side\"]','2',NULL,1,2,'2025-10-08 11:58:55.651000','03df8683f297479395dcaaa941564c91'),('38a6f199f2e247d39239f4590df5ba3d','According to the core concepts, what is the distinction between `null` and `undefined` data types?','mcq','[\"`null` means a variable has not been declared, while `undefined` means it has no value.\", \"`null` is an intentional absence of any object value, while `undefined` means a variable has been declared but not yet assigned a value.\", \"`null` is a `string` type, while `undefined` is a `number` type.\", \"`null` is used for errors, while `undefined` is for successful operations.\"]','1',NULL,1,5,'2025-10-08 13:25:59.717000','b5632b45519049c494b634084e77c2a8'),('394aee8180874d29bc75c0320378ca4d','According to the text, what is the primary role of Trigonometric Identities?','mcq','[\"To define the sides of a right triangle.\", \"To simplify complex trigonometric expressions.\", \"To pinpoint exact moments within cyclical patterns.\", \"To measure the amplitude of a wave.\"]','1',NULL,1,1,'2025-10-10 08:28:03.946169','71afc962f2104a6abeb7d480f6c4dd80'),('395e6d51a2204be28f5c73cc34bcd96d','What is the defining characteristic of a right triangle?','mcq','[\"It has three equal sides.\", \"It contains one angle that measures exactly 90 degrees.\", \"All of its angles are acute.\", \"Its longest side is always opposite an acute angle.\"]','1',NULL,1,1,'2025-10-08 17:01:49.724000','a7fb522bd62546d9b06810a8c5579b76'),('3a9982dd13144bd4a1221ee499a756be','If the non-homogeneous term `f(x)` in the equation `a y\'\' + b y\' + c y = f(x)` were equal to 0, what type of ODE would it become?','mcq','[\"A first-order ODE\", \"A homogeneous ODE\", \"A non-linear ODE\", \"A partial differential equation\"]','1',NULL,1,5,'2025-10-10 04:22:14.314000','bf188003cab7489f994226630f178712'),('3c933ec74c814673bdb2e3c956e35799','What is the defining characteristic of a right triangle?','mcq','[\"It has three equal sides.\", \"It contains one 90-degree angle.\", \"All its angles are acute.\", \"It has four sides.\"]','1',NULL,1,3,'2025-10-08 11:51:31.646000','1a3b7e637fb445fa9d533dc78e3a6ced'),('3ce4aa16de6f4eb199878f336b4d50de','On a unit circle, what does sin(x) represent?','mcq','[\"The x-coordinate of the point corresponding to angle x.\", \"The y-coordinate of the point corresponding to angle x.\", \"The hypotenuse of the right-angled triangle formed by angle x.\", \"The slope of the line from the origin to the point corresponding to angle x.\"]','1',NULL,1,2,'2025-10-10 08:28:04.083322','0b70b73bb0724d8ab38231710baff8ad'),('3d0cef163bed4fa685549d80a51f4975','According to the introduction, what is Right Triangle Trigonometry primarily described as?','mcq','[\"An abstract mathematical theory with no practical use.\", \"A method for drawing perfect triangles.\", \"A practical toolkit for solving real-world problems involving distances, heights, and angles.\", \"A way to identify the color of a triangle.\"]','2',NULL,1,3,'2025-10-08 17:01:49.737000','a7fb522bd62546d9b06810a8c5579b76'),('3ff01f7d91e34fe2a7353d0fe90906f0','What is the defining characteristic of a right triangle?','mcq','[\"All angles are equal.\", \"It has one angle exactly 90 degrees.\", \"It has three acute angles.\", \"All sides are of different lengths.\"]','1',NULL,1,1,'2025-10-10 08:28:03.577338','d9c56dcdae694234b4c12ff647854293'),('412b1acf7b6b4936aae754ed0347ebe1','The content states that Django Apps are \"designed to be reusable and can be plugged into different Django projects.\" What does this primarily imply about their design?','mcq','[\"Apps must contain their own database and user authentication system.\", \"Apps are built to be independent of specific project-level configurations and can function across various projects.\", \"Apps are only useful for very small, single-feature websites.\", \"Apps automatically handle all URL routing for the entire project.\"]','1',NULL,1,4,'2025-10-08 16:49:32.804000','ab9fc04dfb08474b81448a4cd33f8167'),('424090d074244b98b22f50c7600aba58','Which mechanism allows a component to manage its own internal data that can change over time, leading to updates in the UI?','mcq','[\"Props\", \"State\", \"Context\", \"Reducers\"]','1',NULL,1,2,'2025-10-08 13:12:16.852000','ff8aac3e77954f00aa8104edb373050c'),('425e0617125e439ca006a6756aeccb02','What is the defining characteristic of the Unit Circle?','mcq','[\"It has a radius of 360 units.\", \"It is centered at any point on the coordinate plane.\", \"It has a radius of exactly 1 unit and is centered at the origin (0,0).\", \"Its circumference is always 1 unit.\"]','2',NULL,1,1,'2025-10-08 11:51:31.731000','759235b9d57a406fb2d43c1b09ddb086'),('440cb7bedd48498fab1db26e8823ca64','One of the key advantages of `useState` mentioned is that it simplifies stateful logic. How does it achieve this compared to previous methods?','mcq','[\"By requiring developers to use `this` binding for state updates.\", \"By allowing state to be added directly to functional components with a straightforward function call, eliminating complexities like `this` binding and class-specific syntax.\", \"By enforcing the use of complex inheritance hierarchies for state management.\", \"By making state management exclusive to parent components.\"]','1',NULL,1,5,'2025-10-08 13:12:16.934000','c07d62f459584f95ae7f68eeb706d841'),('49a9b9777e8b45b09cf769a8dc4c7a00','What is the primary role of differential equations in applied mathematics, according to the text?','mcq','[\"To solve for static numerical values.\", \"To describe rates of change and model dynamic processes.\", \"To analyze geometric shapes.\", \"To perform complex algebraic manipulations.\"]','1',NULL,1,1,'2025-10-10 04:11:14.251000','aae4ce9acb1c4afeba814726a675d550'),('4b34330e3632450584546cab5cbed70f','In a right triangle, which side is always the longest and directly opposite the 90-degree angle?','mcq','[\"The Adjacent Side\", \"A Leg\", \"The Hypotenuse\", \"The Opposite Side\"]','2',NULL,1,2,'2025-10-10 08:28:03.597867','d9c56dcdae694234b4c12ff647854293'),('4f184ab2d2264db99f6c3fe0c04dc93d','What is the radian measure for half a circle (180 degrees)?','mcq','[\"2 * pi radians\", \"pi / 2 radians\", \"pi radians\", \"360 radians\"]','2',NULL,1,3,'2025-10-10 08:28:03.777775','3923bddcbc8a412fae18621ffcdbbd4c'),('4ff95ff4bb104ca3877bd37e792ea5ed','Based on the general form a(x)y\'\' + b(x)y\' + c(x)y = f(x), which of the following represents a Second-Order Linear Homogeneous ODE?','mcq','[\"y\'\' + xy\' + y^2 = 0\", \"x^2y\'\' + sin(x)y\' + 3y = 0\", \"y\'\' + y\'y = 0\", \"y\'\' + 2y\' + y = x\"]','1',NULL,1,5,'2025-10-10 04:22:14.285000','0a43196b3ca94ea9b55f955d79081eb5'),('51b3c6f52e12411d8f35fdfeaf7383df','According to the learning guide, what is the primary purpose of Trigonometry in solving real-world problems?','mcq','[\"To directly measure all sides and angles of any triangle.\", \"To determine unknown lengths and angles indirectly.\", \"To prove the Pythagorean theorem.\", \"To only measure acute angles in right triangles.\"]','1',NULL,1,4,'2025-10-08 11:47:29.017000','64a5ab1b9a8e4be3b8592d4fcbf8f20d'),('5306c5628db74d698871ba0a0af13c88','How is the \"order\" of a differential equation determined?','mcq','[\"By the number of independent variables present.\", \"By the highest derivative present in the equation.\", \"By the number of functions involved in the equation.\", \"By whether it describes a linear or non-linear system.\"]','1',NULL,1,2,'2025-10-08 12:21:30.305000','1c18e83623634608a445f8410a760a8c'),('57c428c221d44ce591b04e9977250780','In the context of differential equations, what is the key characteristic that defines an Ordinary Differential Equation (ODE)?','mcq','[\"It involves functions of multiple independent variables.\", \"It relates an unknown function to its partial derivatives.\", \"It involves functions of a single independent variable and their ordinary derivatives.\", \"It always has a constant solution.\"]','2',NULL,1,2,'2025-10-10 04:11:14.260000','aae4ce9acb1c4afeba814726a675d550'),('584f626494d541ffbb96a4103ae080d0','Which of the following best describes an angle?','mcq','[\"A single line extending infinitely in one direction.\", \"A point where two lines intersect.\", \"Formed by two rays that share a common endpoint.\", \"A closed two-dimensional shape with three sides.\"]','2',NULL,1,3,'2025-10-08 11:47:28.902000','491ae6426cb347c5b61af6bdbc1e92b2'),('59d0d9691b46411cbddd858c0e07547f','How does the definition of cos(x) on a unit circle differ from sin(x)?','mcq','[\"cos(x) is the y-coordinate, while sin(x) is the x-coordinate.\", \"cos(x) is the x-coordinate, while sin(x) is the y-coordinate.\", \"cos(x) is the ratio of opposite to hypotenuse, while sin(x) is adjacent to hypotenuse.\", \"cos(x) is always positive, while sin(x) can be negative.\"]','1',NULL,1,4,'2025-10-10 08:28:04.136798','0b70b73bb0724d8ab38231710baff8ad'),('5b22043203424bb7b8b923e189404a70','How do React Hooks, specifically `useState` and `useEffect`, empower functional components compared to their pre-Hooks state?','mcq','[\"They allow functional components to use `this` binding.\", \"They enable functional components to manage state and perform side effects, capabilities previously reserved for class components.\", \"They force all components to be written as pure functions without any internal logic.\", \"They introduce complex inheritance hierarchies for state management.\"]','1',NULL,1,4,'2025-10-08 13:12:16.932000','c07d62f459584f95ae7f68eeb706d841'),('5e53a78c7c304cc3b730eb21d5733414','Which of the following types of differential equations often require advanced techniques like Laplace Transforms or Series Solutions?','mcq','[\"Linear equations with constant coefficients and continuous forcing functions.\", \"Equations with discontinuous forcing functions.\", \"Equations that can be solved using characteristic equations.\", \"Equations solvable by undetermined coefficients.\"]','1',NULL,1,3,'2025-10-10 04:22:14.377000','580ab48eb18e4e8baee457a0401cc668'),('60e0bdaa32e84afa9ca9a546257dd6af','In a right triangle, the \"Adjacent Side\" is defined as the side next to the specific acute angle of focus. What other condition must it meet?','mcq','[\"It must be the longest side.\", \"It must be opposite the 90-degree angle.\", \"It must *not* be the hypotenuse.\", \"It must be shorter than the opposite side.\"]','2',NULL,1,5,'2025-10-08 17:01:49.741000','a7fb522bd62546d9b06810a8c5579b76'),('61310250091e4242ae757b8b5cd76305','When identifying the \"opposite\" and \"adjacent\" sides in a right triangle, what is crucial to remember?','mcq','[\"They always stay the same regardless of the angle.\", \"They only change if the triangle is rotated.\", \"They change depending on which acute angle you are focusing on.\", \"They are only relevant for the hypotenuse.\"]','2',NULL,1,4,'2025-10-08 11:58:55.655000','03df8683f297479395dcaaa941564c91'),('64997a62c93644cf8ed522e3614c0e6a','In trigonometry, when an angle is in standard position, where is its vertex located?','mcq','[\"Along the positive x-axis.\", \"At the origin (0,0).\", \"Anywhere on the circumference of the Unit Circle.\", \"At the point (1,0).\"]','1',NULL,1,2,'2025-10-08 11:51:31.732000','759235b9d57a406fb2d43c1b09ddb086'),('64beda5d59e145ff81c794a2e39eeeef','When a differential equation is described as \"Ordinary,\" what does this imply about the unknown function?','mcq','[\"It depends on multiple independent variables.\", \"It depends on only one independent variable.\", \"It is always a linear function.\", \"It has no derivatives higher than the first.\"]','1',NULL,1,2,'2025-10-10 04:12:08.146000','90d62550c0d54237947475f5e801a6f6'),('6593c211b83f42ec93f792f39e13948b','In the first-order ODE `dT/dt = -k(T - T_a)`, identify the dependent and independent variables.','mcq','[\"T is independent, t is dependent.\", \"t is independent, T is dependent.\", \"k is independent, T_a is dependent.\", \"T and t are both dependent.\"]','1',NULL,1,4,'2025-10-10 04:11:14.267000','aae4ce9acb1c4afeba814726a675d550'),('669d6ebb9cbe4aba88f3003bf8ba9412','Which formula is used to convert a degree measure to radians?','mcq','[\"Multiply the degree measure by 180 / pi.\", \"Multiply the degree measure by pi / 360.\", \"Multiply the degree measure by pi / 180.\", \"Multiply the degree measure by 2 * pi.\"]','2',NULL,1,4,'2025-10-10 08:28:03.785768','3923bddcbc8a412fae18621ffcdbbd4c'),('66c0830b1e794c5e8492e4d8a5d7cc60','In the context of a second-order ODE `a y\'\' + b y\' + c y = f(x)`, what term makes the equation \"non-homogeneous\"?','mcq','[\"The dependent variable 